add('9:e-i',['A3.3.3','A3.3.4'],'FEEDBACK(Category,Score) initially contains ("repair",2),("repair",4),("paint",5). A service first runs SELECT AVG(Score) FROM FEEDBACK WHERE Category=\'repair\'; and stores its result, then INSERT INTO FEEDBACK(Category,Score) VALUES(\'repair\',5);. Describe the stored result and the effect of the INSERT, explaining whether the stored result includes the new row.','The stored average is3 from scores2 and4. INSERT adds the repair score5, producing a third repair row. The already stored result remains3 because the SELECT happened before insertion; a fresh average would be11/3.',[(1,'Stored average3.'),(1,'Explains only pre-insert repair rows counted.'),(1,'Correct new row added.'),(1,'Stored value unchanged unless the query is rerun.')],[28],status='B',adapt='Retains original aggregate-before-insertion reasoning; removes PHP/CGI mechanics and evaluates explicit SQL effects.',ms_summary='Original server computes existing category average, inserts submitted rating, compares new rating against old average and outputs a corresponding message.',test_code='''import sqlite3
c=sqlite3.connect(':memory:');c.executescript("CREATE TABLE Feedback(Category,Score);INSERT INTO Feedback VALUES('repair',2),('repair',4),('paint',5);")
avg=c.execute("SELECT AVG(Score) FROM Feedback WHERE Category='repair'").fetchone()[0]
c.execute("INSERT INTO Feedback VALUES('repair',5)")
assert avg==3 and c.execute("SELECT COUNT(*) FROM Feedback WHERE Category='repair'").fetchone()[0]==3''',check='SQLite aggregate-before-insert and final row count executed.')
