add('11:d',['A2.1.2'],'A company can keep all computing on equipment it buys and manages, or rent cloud computing/storage with rapid capacity changes and a provider-managed physical infrastructure. Evaluate the cloud choice for a seasonal service handling confidential records.','Cloud capacity can expand for seasonal peaks and contract afterwards, avoiding permanent purchase for rare demand. The provider manages physical infrastructure, reducing local maintenance. However, the company depends on connectivity/provider availability and must configure access controls and assess confidentiality obligations. Choose cloud only where those controls and service arrangements meet the records’ needs; elasticity alone does not settle the decision.',[(1,'Elastic capacity linked to seasonal demand.'),(1,'Cost/maintenance benefit developed.'),(1,'Connectivity/provider dependence.'),(1,'Confidentiality/access-control responsibility developed.'),(1,'Supported contextual decision.')],[34,35,36],status='B',adapt='Provides infrastructure facts and evaluates purpose/benefits/limits; memorized private/public/hybrid cloud taxonomies are not imposed.')
